30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems the current allocation has been stagnant for years without review. Also, charging fees can create social friction and isolation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that the same people have had the best spots for five years! But some daily riders are actually okay with paying.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The physical layout is a problem. People are shifting bikes to get out, and some spots are exposed to rain, making them less desirable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our building account is nearly empty, and the local ward park is expensive and full. We can't simply tell people to park elsewhere.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I've looked into the labor. Managing payments is already time-consuming, and high-tech racks require physical maintenance that we might neglect.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, if the account is empty, a paid system might seem attractive, but as I saw from the neighbors, it can ruin community ties.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But if the daily riders want to pay to ensure they have a spot, isn't that fair?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Fairness isn't just about money. If the spots are uneven in quality due to rain, a simple lottery or payment doesn't fix the ""shoving match.""","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, a ""shoving match"" is just a lack of discipline. However, the fact that people are willing to pay is a useful lever.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,We must consider who does the work. Adding more billing to the treasurer's load is a recipe for the system collapsing.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"A lottery would be neutral, but it doesn't solve the physical congestion Ryuji mentioned.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,What about the racks? Would that stop the fighting?,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Only if they are easy to use. If they are cumbersome, we'll just have new problems.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be rational. We have a lack of funds, a lack of space, and a lack of administrative will.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. Any system requiring monthly bookkeeping or mechanical upkeep is risky.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We need a balance between fairness, social harmony, and sustainability.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I just want the people who use their bikes every day to be happy!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'm leaning toward a system that removes ""ownership"" of a specific spot to end the disputes.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm curious to see the options, but I suspect a paid model is the only one that actually benefits the building.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for the option that requires the least amount of ongoing human effort.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is too risky for our community spirit. Option C sounds efficient, but I worry about the physical struggle of using them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option A helps the people who really need the bikes, and it gives us money! But Option C sounds like it would be fair for everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C solves the ""ownership"" and ""shoving"" issue by making it first-come, first-served. However, double-tier racks can be a pain to use.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only one that addresses the building's empty coffers. It's a market solution to a scarcity problem.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is an administrative nightmare. Option C requires mechanical maintenance. Option B is a simple once-a-year event.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, you prefer the lottery because it's low-effort?","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,But a lottery means some people might get a bad spot for a whole year!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"A lottery doesn't stop the morning congestion. Shared racks (C) are the only way to stop people from fighting over ""their"" spot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you're overestimating the ""congestion."" A paid system (A) ensures those who value the space most are the ones using it.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I cannot support A. The treasurer is already overwhelmed. B is the most sustainable from a labor perspective.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm torn. B is fair and low-conflict, but C is more modern. Given the neighbor's experience, I'll avoid A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I like the idea of shared racks! It feels like we're all in this together.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'll go with C. It's the only one that fundamentally changes the behavior in the parking area.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all ignoring the financial benefit of A. But if you're all going to be sentimental, I'll consider the most efficient alternative.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Efficiency is not just about the result, but the cost of maintenance. B is the only one that doesn't create a new chore.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for B. It's the safest for our social dynamics.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'll vote for C! Let's try the racks!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,C is my choice. Let's fix the physical problem.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since A is outvoted by sentiment, I'll vote C. It's more rational than a random lottery.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I stick with B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
